SCAN-Planner numerical core
Source: https://github.com/wuyi2121/SCAN-Planner
Upstream main commit: 348e8a5 (add: sensor layout)
Authors: Han Zheng, Zhe Chen, Yiwen Fu, Ming Yang, Tong Qin
License: Apache-2.0; embedded L-BFGS retains its own license header.

Local adaptation for simulation_new (2026-10-26):
- Replace ROS parameters and timing with C++ options and steady deadlines.
- Inject a request-local static-world occupancy interface. Preserve projected
  XY A-star guidance and locked-Z spline optimization.
- Bound visited A-star nodes, allocate them lazily, and release search storage.
- Replace variable-length stack arrays; support fixed endpoint control counts.
- Observe deadlines in optimization/search and reject timed-out results.
- Suppress routine solver console output; retain failure diagnostics.
- Correct stale A-star priority entries on decreased cost and its initial score.
- Follow the supplied terrain reference for projected A-star heights and endpoint
  adjustment, preserving stair landings instead of imposing a straight Z plane.
The upstream robot, sensors, mapping frontend, navigation FSM and controllers
are not included.
